  "reason": "Evidence: The strongest direction is clearly multimodal scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l (config_036: 0.715, config_037: 0.706, config_038: 0.721). Within this family, we have a 2×2 grid of aggregation (avgpool/transformer) × fusion (concat/weighted) with three of four cells filled. The missing cell is transformer + weighted (config_039). Current evidence suggests concat > weighted (0.715 vs 0.706) and transformer ≥ avgpool (0.721 vs 0.715), but each comparison rests on a single data point. Question tested: Does the weighted-fusion penalty persist under transformer aggregation, or does transformer aggregation mitigate the information loss from weighted fusion? This clarifies whether the interaction between aggregation and fusion is significant or whether the main effects (prefer concat, prefer transformer) are sufficient. Why best next experiment: Completing this small factorial design is the highest-information, lowest-risk use of the next budget slot. It sits squarely in the proven best-performing region, will yield a configuration likely near 0.71+, and will give a definitive recommendation on the aggregation×fusion choice for the final architecture without the uncertainty of jumping to an untested dimension (e.g., resnet50 image encoder, which performed poorly standalone at 0.208)."
}

